OpenBSD has no NSS, so the nss-mdns lookup can never succeed and the
startup warning is just noise. Keep nss_support (still reported over D-Bus
by dbus-protocol.c) at its default of 0.

Index: avahi-daemon/main.c
--- avahi-daemon/main.c.orig
+++ avahi-daemon/main.c
@@ -1163,8 +1163,10 @@ static int run_server(DaemonConfig *c) {
 
     ignore_signal(SIGPIPE);
 
+#ifndef __OpenBSD__
     if (!(nss_support = avahi_nss_support()))
         avahi_log_warn("WARNING: No NSS support for mDNS detected, consider installing nss-mdns!");
+#endif
 
     if (!(simple_poll_api = avahi_simple_poll_new())) {
         avahi_log_error("Failed to create main loop object.");
